{"name":"Trojan Horse Brown","hex":"#775020","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trojan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Malware that appears to perform or actually performs a desired task for a user while performing a harmful task without the user's knowledge or consent."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Describing a satellite (moon or minor planet) that shares an orbit with another"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trojan"},{"term":"horse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hoofed mammal, Equus ferus caballus, often used throughout history for riding and draft work.","Any member of the species Equus ferus, including the Przewalski's horse and the extinct Equus ferus ferus."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Synonym of horse around.","To play mischievous pranks on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horse"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trojan Horse","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, the Trojan Horse was a wooden horse said to have been used by the Greeks during the Trojan War to sneak into the city of Troy and win the war. The Trojan Horse is not mentioned in Homer's Iliad, with the poem ending before the war is concluded, and it is only briefly mentioned in the Odyssey. It is described at length in the Aeneid, in which Virgil recounts how, after a fruitless ten-year siege, the Greeks constructed a huge wooden horse at the behest of Odysseus, and hid a select force of men inside, including Odysseus himself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Mykonos_vase.jpg/330px-Mykonos_vase.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trojan_Horse"},{"title":"Horse","blocks":[{"text":"The horse is a domesticated, one-toed, hoofed mammal. It belongs to the taxonomic family Equidae and is one of two extant subspecies of Equus ferus. The horse has evolved over the past 45 to 55 million years from a small multi-toed creature, Eohippus, into the large single-toed animal of today, originally in North America. Humans began domesticating horses around 4000 BCE in Central Asia, primarily associated with the Botai culture; their domestication is believed to have been widespread by 3000 BCE. However, contemporary genetic evidence indicates that modern domesticated breeds do not descend from this lineage, instead pointing to the Western Eurasian steppes in the lower Volga-Don region as the homeland of modern domestic horses. The modern horse breed replaced the local populations through their rapid expansion across Eurasia from 2000 BCE. Horses in the subspecies caballus are domesticated, although some domesticated populations live in the wild as feral horses. These feral populations are not true wild horses, which are horses that have never been domesticated. There is an extensive, specialized vocabulary used to describe equine-related concepts, covering everything from anatomy to life stages, size, colors, markings, breeds, locomotion, and behavior."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg/330px-Nokota_Horses_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horse"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca